# Nuclear OpenSpec before implementation (non-negotiable)

**Never start implementing an OpenSpec change until `nuclear-openspec` has been
run on that change and High findings are resolved (or explicitly deferred in the
OpenSpec with rationale).**

This is the plan-time gate. Code nuclear (`nuclear-branch`) comes later at PR
time — see `nuclear-branch-before-pr.mdc`.

## When it applies

- User asks to implement / continue / apply an OpenSpec change (`openspec-apply`,
  `/opsx:apply`, “start phase N”, “implement tasks”)
- Agent is about to mark the first task `[x]` or write production code for a
  change under `openspec/changes/<name>/`
- After a **material design rewrite** (goals, security model, or task graph
  changed) — re-run before more implementation

## Agent workflow

1. Identify the change name (`openspec/changes/<name>/`).
2. Read and follow `.cursor/skills/nuclear-openspec/SKILL.md`.
3. Produce the nuclear-openspec verdict in the conversation (or confirm a prior
   run in this thread still matches current artifacts).
4. If verdict is **Amend then implement** or **Re-scope**: update OpenSpec
   artifacts first; do **not** write feature code until High gaps are closed or
   explicitly deferred in `design.md` / `tasks.md` with rationale.
5. Confirm `design.md` has a **Threat model** section (or documented skim for
   trivial doc-only) per `docs/quality-evidence.md` and
   `.cursor/skills/nuclear-openspec/SKILL.md`.
6. Only then proceed with `openspec-apply` / implementation.

## Exceptions (narrow)

- User explicitly says to skip nuclear-openspec for this change (quote that in
  the reply).
- Trivial doc-only OpenSpec with no behaviour/security surface — still skim
  lens C; say why a full nuclear was not needed.
- Re-applying after nuclear already passed in **this** conversation and
  proposal/design/specs/tasks are unchanged.

## Never

- Skip straight from `openspec-propose` to coding without nuclear-openspec.
- Treat “tasks look clear” as a substitute for the skill.
- Mark High security/correctness design gaps as “fix in implementation.”
